The starlink.html 3D globe lacked mobile interactivity, geographic context, and user guidance.

## Changes

**Mobile touch controls:**
- Added pinch-to-zoom gesture support (two-finger detection with distance tracking)
- Set `touch-action: none` to prevent browser scroll interference
- Call `preventDefault()` on touch events to avoid page scroll conflicts during globe interaction

**Country borders:**
- Added 18 major countries rendered as electric blue lines on globe surface
- Lat/lon coordinates converted to 3D sphere positions using spherical-to-Cartesian transform

**Info overlay:**
- Persistent panel showing satellite count (9,400+), coverage, orbit altitude
- Platform-specific instructions (desktop: drag/scroll, mobile: swipe/pinch)
- Responsive layout: full-width on mobile, fixed-width on desktop

**Code quality:**
- Extracted zoom constants (`ZOOM_MIN`, `ZOOM_MAX`, `ZOOM_SPEED_WHEEL`, `ZOOM_SPEED_PINCH`)

## Key implementation

Touch handling differentiates between rotation and zoom:

```javascript
container.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (e.touches.length === 2) {
        // Two-finger: prepare pinch zoom
        const dx = e.touches[0].clientX - e.touches[1].clientX;
        const dy = e.touches[0].clientY - e.touches[1].clientY;
        lastTouchDistance = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
    } else if (e.touches.length === 1) {
        // Single finger: rotate globe
        isDragging = true;
        previousMousePosition = { x: e.touches[0].clientX, y: e.touches[0].clientY };
    }
});
```

